data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":657,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_094b5dd7ada33d2d016adb3214b2c48191a98d9549d07c01a9","call_id":"call_97779ad5c39440678e57fe0cf8768221","name":"submit_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"target_review\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The frozen problem statement and source-context agree on the complete theorem: arbitrary prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer 0<=lambda<p, and arbitrary admissible lattice M, with V(K)=M tensor_Z K and irreducibility for the Chevalley action. H001-H004 supply precisely these data; lambda=0 and p=2 are included. The conclusion spells out nonzero and invariant-subspace meaning. No source restriction to a preferred lattice or distinct-weight premise is added.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"problem.md:3\\\",\\\"source-context.md:14-45\\\",\\\"spec.json:/full_target,/conclusion,/hypotheses\\\",\\\"nl0.json:/propositions/4 (P statement)\\\"]},\\\"definition_reviews\\\":{},\\\"source_reviews\\\":{},\\\"structure_review\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Bipartite graph has all four frozen H roots and one inference R001 producing the sole target P; every H is a direct input and there are no retained disconnected propositions, internal nodes, E/M nodes, or global D definitions. Thus AND closure has no missing graph edge/producer. There are no M declarations/applications, so no pinned mathlib declaration is implicated. The single inference body is visible and reviewed for global consistency; this is not a per-inference packet replay.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"nl0.json:/propositions\\\",\\\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/inputs\\\",\\\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/output\\\",\\\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument\\\"]},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"nl0.json:/inferences/0/argument/0-4, especially S004-S005\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Notation for the reduced basis is not consistently closed in the exact proof. S004 establishes that the R-basis is (a e_i), and that the reduced module has the corresponding basis. S005 then treats the e_i as that reduced basis (writes w=sum c_i e_i and concludes e_j in W), although e_i were defined in characteristic zero in S001; neither their membership in M_R nor an identification of their reductions with the basis (a e_i) is established. The generator a is an arbitrary generator of J and is not shown to be a unit, so this cannot be inferred by identifying e_i with a e_i. One can likely repair this by using a e_i throughout S005 and explaining the induced matrix units, but Audit A must preserve the frozen candidate and cannot silently make that repair. This blocks the exact proof's target-edge argument; no claimed proof pass. The requested stage excludes packet replay, which was not performed.\\\"},{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"signature-evidence.json:1; spec.json:/definitions; nl0.json:/propositions,/inferences\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"There are no D or M IDs in the exact candidate, hence the keyed definition/source review maps are empty. The separate signature-evidence document is empty. No mathlib source probe or pinned-source declaration review is applicable or available; no theorem is treated as certified by it.\\\"}]}\"}","status":"completed"}}

